1
00:02:27,638 --> 00:02:29,226
<v MAN> Good morning.Can I help you?

2
00:02:29,226 --> 00:02:37,515
<v WOMAN> Yes.I've just been accepted on a course at the university and I'd like to try and arrange accommodation in the hall of residence.

3
00:02:37,515 --> 00:02:45,058
<v MAN> Yes, certainly. Please sit down. What I'll do is fill in a form with you to find out a little more about your preferences and so forth.

4
00:02:45,058 --> 00:02:45,790
<v WOMAN> Thank you.

5
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:49,141
<v MAN> So first of all, can I take your name?

6
00:02:49,141 --> 00:02:50,957
<v WOMAN> It's Anu Bhatt.

7
00:02:50,957 --> 00:02:52,258
<v MAN> Could you spell your name please?

8
00:02:52,258 --> 00:02:58,782
<v WOMAN> Yes.A-N-U...B-H-A double T.

9
00:02:58,782 --> 00:03:01,476
<v MAN> Thanks, and could I ask your date of birth?

10
00:03:01,476 --> 00:03:04,936
<v WOMAN> 31st March 1972.

11
00:03:04,936 --> 00:03:07,302
<v MAN> Thank you. And where are you from?

12
00:03:07,302 --> 00:03:08,003
<v WOMAN> India.

13
00:03:08,003 --> 00:03:11,327
<v MAN> Oh right.And what will you be studying?

14
00:03:11,327 --> 00:03:13,616
<v WOMAN> I'm doing a course in nursing.

15
00:03:13,616 --> 00:03:18,218
<v MAN> Right, thank you. And how long would you want to stay in hall, do you think?

16
00:03:18,218 --> 00:03:28,129
<v WOMAN> Well, it'll take three years but I'd only like to stay in hall for two. I'd like to think about living outside for the third year.

17
00:03:28,129 --> 00:03:36,211
<v MAN> Fine. And what did you have in mind for catering? Do you want to cook for yourself or have all your meals provided, that's full board?

18
00:03:36,211 --> 00:03:38,658
<v WOMAN> Is there something in between?

19
00:03:38,658 --> 00:03:42,445
<v MAN> Yes. You can just have evening meal provided, which is half board.

20
00:03:42,445 --> 00:03:44,337
<v WOMAN> That's what I'd prefer.

21
00:03:44,337 --> 00:03:51,757
<v MAN> Yes, a lot of students opt for that. Now, with that in mind, do you have any special diet, anything we should know about?

22
00:03:51,757 --> 00:03:54,919
<v WOMAN> Yes, I don't take red meat.

23
00:03:54,919 --> 00:03:58,071
<v MAN> No red meat.

24
00:04:44,167 --> 00:05:04,908
<v MAN> Now, thinking about the room itself, we have a number of options. You can have a single study bedroom or you can have a shared one. These are both what we call simple rooms. The other alternative is to opt for a single bedsit which actually has more space and better facilities. There's about ￡20 a week difference between them.

25
00:05:04,908 --> 00:05:10,802
<v WOMAN> Well, actually my grant is quite generous and I think the bedsit sounds the best option.

26
00:05:10,802 --> 00:05:19,124
<v MAN> Lovely. I'll put you down for that and we'll see what availability is like. Now can I ask some other personal details which we like to have on record?

27
00:05:19,124 --> 00:05:20,338
<v WOMAN> Yes, of course.

28
00:05:20,338 --> 00:05:27,409
<v MAN> I wonder if you could let us know what your interests are. This might help us get a closer match for placing you in a particular hall.

29
00:05:27,409 --> 00:05:31,265
<v WOMAN> Ummm. Well. I love the theatre.

30
00:05:31,265 --> 00:05:32,390
<v MAN> Right.

31
00:05:32,390 --> 00:05:36,237
<v WOMAN> And I enjoy sports, particularly badminton.

32
00:05:36,237 --> 00:05:46,484
<v MAN> That's worth knowing. Now, what we finish with on the form is really a list from you of what your priorities are in choosing a hall and we'll do our best to take these into account.

33
00:05:46,484 --> 00:05:53,637
<v WOMAN> Well, the first thing is I'd prefer a hall where there are other mature students, if possible.

34
00:05:53,637 --> 00:05:57,595
<v MAN> Yes, we do have halls which tend to cater for slightly older students.

35
00:05:57,595 --> 00:06:02,571
<v WOMAN> Ummm and I'd prefer to be out of town.

36
00:06:02,571 --> 00:06:07,240
<v MAN> That's actually very good for you because we tend to have more vacancies in out-of -town halls.

37
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,498
<v WOMAN> Lucky!

38
00:06:08,498 --> 00:06:10,785
<v MAN> Yes. Anything else?

39
00:06:10,785 --> 00:06:19,442
<v WOMAN> Well, I would like somewhere with a shared area, a TV room for example, or something like that. It's a good way to socialise.

40
00:06:19,442 --> 00:06:20,319
<v MAN> It certainly is.

41
00:06:20,319 --> 00:06:21,331
<v WOMAN> That's it.

42
00:06:21,331 --> 00:06:24,617
<v MAN> Now, we just need a contact telephone number for you.

43
00:06:24,617 --> 00:06:33,473
<v WOMAN> Sure, I'll just find it. It's double 67549.

44
00:06:33,473 --> 00:06:37,159
<v MAN> Great, so we'll be in contact with you as soon as possible...